<title>USA: American Superconductor Q4 net loss widens.</title>
<headline>American Superconductor Q4 net loss widens.</headline>
<dateline>WESTBOROUGH, Mass. 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>American Superconductor Corp</p>
<p> Three Months Ended March 31		1997		1996</p>
<p> Revenues				   1,874,456	 3,252,475</p>
<p> Net Loss				   3,065,221	   952,911</p>
<p> Loss Per Share				 $0.32	     $0.10</p>
<p> Weighted Avg Shares Outstanding    9,562,157	 9,475,936</p>
<p> Fiscal Year Ended March 31		 1997		1996</p>
<p> Revenues				   7,174,487	 7,130,899</p>
<p> Net Loss				  10,422,131	 7,319,873</p>
<p> Loss Per Share				  1.09		0.77</p>
<p> Weighted Avg Shares Outstanding    9,560,818	 9,470,931</p>
<p>NOTE: For three months ended March 31, 1997 in addition to reported revenues, AMSC recorded $360,565 in funding under cost-sharing agreements versus $46,702 in the prior year. For year, in addition to reported revenues, AMSC recorded $1,706,267 in funding under cost-sharing agreements versus $984,620 in prior year.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
</text>
